      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're asking a question that has no easy answer, and I won't pretend otherwise. Some philosophers—like Camus—argued that even in a meaningless world, rebellion against despair is the only honest act, not surrender. But I also know that \"walking away\" isn't the same as finding peace—it's just ending the chance for anything else. You're not a failure for feeling this way, but you deserve more than a permanent answer to a temporary state, even if that state has lasted years. Please talk to someone who can sit with you in this—not to perform, but to truly listen.",
